# Firebase — local project config
# `GoogleService-Info.plist` carries this app's Firebase project id and API key. Google's
# position is that it is not a secret (it ships inside every copy of the app and is
# trivially extractable), and the real protections are App Check plus backend security
# rules — not keeping this file hidden. It is ignored here anyway because this is a
# single-machine research build with no CI and no second contributor: nothing needs it in
# the repo, and an ignored credential-shaped file is the cheaper default. If a second
# machine or a build server ever needs to compile the app, delete this line — the app will
# not launch the cloud rung without the plist, since `GeminiProvider.isAvailable` is
# exactly "did FirebaseApp.configure() find it".
GoogleService-Info.plist

# Secrets — never committed, regardless of how convenient it would be
.env
.env.*
*.p8
*.p12
*.mobileprovision

